# One file, two calls. Every node of the file is two PLACES in the program,
# named through the site that reaches it, and each place is its own thing:
#
#   one.hold / two.hold   two waits in one run; `weft wake` resolves one at a time
#   one.tick / two.tick   two registered triggers, each with its own display
#   one.key  / two.key    the two names of the file's one access node
#
# The compiler's own key for a node of the file (`@src:lib:part.hold`) is
# refused everywhere a person types a name.

src = Text { value: "hello" }

one = @include("lib/part.weft")
one.text = src.value

two = @include("lib/part.weft")
two.text = src.value

first = Debug
first.data = one.out

second = Debug
second.data = two.out
